Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object fails to distinguish a pair the documented rule requires it to distinguish. The rule says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text". Reply A is: "~~~json\n{\"a\": 1}\n~~~\n{\"b\": 2}". Reply B is: "{\"a\": 1}\n{\"b\": 2}". For Reply A, the tilde fence is a code fence and holds {\"a\":1}, so the rule requires the function to return {\"a\":1}. For Reply B, no fence holds an object, so the rule requires the last top-level object, {\"b\":2}. The function's _FENCE regex only matches three backticks, so it ignores the tilde fence in Reply A and treats both replies as having the same top-level objects; it returns {\"b\":2} for both. The observation that would show this conjecture false is recover_json_object returning {\"a\":1} for Reply A and {\"b\":2} for Reply B.